# Currency Conversion and Policy-Category Alignment Plan

This plan outlines modifications to check policy limits in the **New Expense Report** using the USD-converted value of the expense amount based on the selected currency, and updates the category dropdown options to match the definitions in the **Policy Hub**.

## User Review Required

> [!NOTE]
> - Exchange rates used for real-time validation:
>   - `1 USD = 1.00 USD`
>   - `1 EUR = 1.08 USD`
>   - `1 GBP = 1.27 USD`
>   - `1 INR = 0.012 USD`
> - Receipt uploads will be required if the converted expense amount exceeds `$25.00 USD`.

## Proposed Changes

---

### Frontend Components

#### [MODIFY] [SubmitExpenseTab.tsx](file:///d:/vibe%20code/spend-managment/project/frontend/src/features/expenses/SubmitExpenseTab.tsx)
- Define a local FX rate mapper (`FX_RATES`) mapping supported currencies (`USD`, `EUR`, `GBP`, `INR`) to their USD conversion rate.
- Update the policy evaluation `useEffect` to:
  - Calculate `amountInUsd` using the selected currency rate.
  - Evaluate daily meals ($50 daily, $15 sub-limit MKT-22), travel ($500), client relations ($150), and office supplies ($200) policies against `amountInUsd`.
  - Add `formData.currency` to the dependency array.
- Update the `handleSubmit` receipt validation to evaluate the `$25 USD` receipt requirement against `amountInUsd`.
- Rename the select dropdown categories to match the Policy Hub:
  - `Meals & Entertainment Cap (Limit $15/$50)`
  - `Business Travel Allowance (Limit $500)`
  - `Client Relations & Entertainment (Limit $150)`
  - `Office Supplies & Hardware (Limit $200)`

